{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/72337-forsaken-antagonists","id":72337,"title":"Forsaken Antagonists","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-14T17:29:27-08:00","id":72337,"title":"Forsaken Antagonists","content":"With the Idigam Chronicles right around the around the proverbial corner I thought it would be a fun exercise to share ideas for antagonists. Obviously the Idigam are going to get the bulk of the development stick, but let's not forget the other baddies.<br /> Do you have an idea for a villain? Throw it out there. <br /> Is there one that already exists that you love? Share your experiences.<br /> Do you think there are some that need more development in particular? Go ahead and talk about it.<br /> <br /> I'll go ahead and throw out one of mine, even though I'll submit he has a silly name: Orcus the Tyrant of Terror. It's a bit of a nod towards my DnD days as well as the name of a god of the underworld, the punisher of broken oaths and the damned. The tormentor of the dead.<br /> <br /> After perusing the various books that discuss the Maeljin, I noticed, much like many others, that there were essentially 7 Deadly Sin Maeljin and then one of Violence and one of Deception. It always seemed to me that there was at least one big archetypal evil that just wasn't touched very well by the 7+2 setup...or maybe I just have a psychological need to make it a round 10. In any case, Orcus is an attempt to create another Maeljin alongside Thurifuge and Pseulak as a demonic spirit lord not tied directly to a single vice.<br /> <br /> Here's some flavor text.<br /> <br /> <i>There is a filthy secret at the heart of power. <br /> A pornographic secret. <br /> Some people don't even need an excuse to wield power. <br /> They won't even say that they're doing it for your own good.<br /> Or that they're doing it to civilize you and your countrymen.<br /> Or to save you from communism.<br /> Or from fascism.<br /> Or from capitalism.<br /> Or even from your own sin.<br /> They do it because they like it.<br /> They're in power because they enjoy punishing people.<br /> They're in power because they enjoy owning people.<br /> They enjoy telling you what you can and cannot do.<br /> They enjoy telling you when they feel like having sex with you and when they don't.<br /> They do this for its own sake.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Tyrannical gods, totalitarian dictators, slave owners and schoolyard bullies. <br /> Not merely fear, but terror.<br /> All consuming terror, corrupting and shackling the mind.<br /> The promise of violence for the slightest criticism.<br /> The promise of torture for any perceived failure.<br /> The promise of everlasting hellfire for not accepting the terms by which they <b>allow </b>you to live.<br /> Anyone who has lived at the graces of another understands what is meant by the word evil.<br /> <br /> There have always been and there will always be those who seek power for the sake of power.<br /> They will make every excuse under the sun to justify it.<br /> They will wield laws and holy books.<br /> To make you think it's deserved.<br /> To make you think it's in your best interests.<br /> To make you compliant.<br /> To bind you with manacles both mind-forged and real.<br /> Until you simply stop resisting.<br /> <br /> They will turn to you and render you complicit.<br /> Dirty you with the filthy secret.<br /> Taint you so you can never be clean again.<br /> Until you simply stop resisting.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T00:00:10-08:00","id":72495,"title":"","content":"In my experience I had some good fortune with a Norse-themed gang called the Fylkning. They were essentially lead by a rune-casting sorcerer who could bind spirits into human bodies, which he used to create stronger soldiers for his gang, and together with an alliance with a spirit lord of crimes it proved to be a rather formidable challenge for the PCs. In the final fight they played it pretty dumb though, and would've been killed if it wasn't for a traitor spirit turning on the Fylkning and using influence to make another one do that as well. Good stuff.<br /> <br /> The end was the gang decimated by Uratha fury, two werewolves down on around 1 or 2 Health levels and one werewolf dead by the end of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, I made the Influence of the Ridden a tad bit more powerful than normal but otherwise the characters would've been butchered outright.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}